Firmware: free-running ("realtime") agent mode for the /agent WebSocket
=====================================================================

Adds an optional {"hold": true} flag to the agent action. With it, the Doom task
does NOT pause between requests: the action's keys stay held while the game keeps
running, each request swaps the held keys and is answered immediately (after one
frame), and `tics` becomes the auto-release timeout (1..175 tics, default 35) so a
vanished controller never leaves the marine walking into a wall. A request
without `hold` (or a disconnect, or 5 s of silence) returns to the existing
behaviour and releases every key the agent was holding. `blocked` in this mode
refers to the previous held action, measured between the two requests with a
threshold that scales with the elapsed tics.

Client side: tools/doom_jev_agent.py --realtime ; tools/doom_agent_sim.py already
emulates it.

Status: written against branch ai-agent-api @ a3cb74b. Builds cleanly with
ESP-IDF v5.5.4 (target esp32p4, your sdkconfig and managed_components: no errors
or warnings in the patched files, app 0x146020 bytes, 68% of the partition free).
